spans.s:
LUṆṬ, Ⅰ. P. luṇṭha, stir up, set 🞄in motion, agitate;
 cs. P. luṇṭhaya, 🞄steal, rob, plunder;
 husk;
 ps. luṇṭhyate, be 🞄stolen: pp. luṇṭhita, stolen, robbed, plundered. 🞄nis, steal, plunder. vi, id.: pp. 🞄rolling about (= vi-luṭhita).

luṇṭh-a, kind of grass;
 -aka, m. plunderer;
 🞄-ana, n. plundering (—˚);
 -āka, m. 🞄robber, plunderer (-tā, f. robbery);
 -i, f. plundering, 🞄pillage.
